7592186347735 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4d59c58c-d76d-581e-8244-df4e793dba6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186347546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347834 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "81c6cb45-6adc-5f19-b537-ff2e27ce7534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346278 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9873e119-5653-5fff-9565-620b8e2698f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80115" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,11,1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩=20.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d51e9464-bbda-5ef7-95c6-2040c203954f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348331 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-5,4⟩ & =20 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z & =20 \\\\ 4z & =20-2x+5y \\\\ z & =5-\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{4}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=2$ and $y=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5-\\frac{1}{2}(2)+\\frac{5}{4}(4)=9.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(2,4,9)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,9⟩-⟨-2,11,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-7,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨2,-5,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(4)\\cdot 2+(-7)\\cdot (-5)+8\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|8+35+32|}{\\sqrt{4+25+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|75|}{\\sqrt{45}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80116" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-6,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩=24.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6801290-8008-514c-8914-c43c32373fba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348332 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,6,3⟩ & =24 \\\\ -8x+6y+3z & =24 \\\\ 3z & =24+8x-6y \\\\ z & =8+\\frac{8}{3}x-2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=3$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=8+\\frac{8}{3}(3)-2(1)=14.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(3,1,14)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,1,14⟩-⟨8,-6,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,7,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-8,6,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot (-8)+7\\cdot 6+9\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|40+42+27|}{\\sqrt{64+36+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|109|}{\\sqrt{109}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80122" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,11,10)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x-4y+4z=16.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0953b145-a938-579d-a5dc-6946f5364a06" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348337 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y+4z & =16 \\\\ -2(2)-4(3)+4z & =16 \\\\ 4z & =32 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,8⟩-⟨-1,11,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-8,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,-4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-2)+(-8)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+32-8|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,18\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80113" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,-4,-8)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,1⟩=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92e09859-2a3a-5255-8ffb-72547639c5f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366351 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,1⟩ & =3 \\\\ -2x+4y+z & =3 \\\\ z & =3+2x-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=3+2(1)-4(1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(1,1,1)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-3,-4,-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,5,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,1⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 4+9\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-8+20+9|}{\\sqrt{4+16+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac